    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d471">

                <pb facs="0555" n="443" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg443"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/5445: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Vladivostok</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Macgowan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vladivostok</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-10-21T15:00:00+08:47"><hi rendition="#italic">October 21,
                                1919, 3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 6:25
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>558. O’Reilly, Acting British High Commissioner, today informed me he had been
                    recalled urgently on account of his attitude toward Kolchak, which I was
                    criticising. Repeated to Tokyo and Omsk.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Macgowan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
